{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"Before making a conditional offer, a housing provider may not ask about or require disclosure of an applicant's criminal record; after an offer it may consider only specified recent or serious convictions, must make an individualized assessment, and may not require drug or alcohol testing.","key_value":"6-year (1st degree), 4-year (2nd/3rd degree), 1-year (4th degree) conviction lookbacks","coverage_conditions":"Any rental dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, except a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; before a conditional offer a housing provider may consider methamphetamine-manufacture convictions in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex-offender registration.","penalty":"Monetary penalty up to $1,000 (no prior violation in 5 years), up to $5,000 (one prior in 5 years) or up to $10,000 (two or more priors in 7 years); director may also order compliance measures and up to $1,000 paid to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether its eligibility criteria include review of criminal history and that the applicant may submit evidence of record inaccuracies, rehabilitation or other mitigating factors.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Any rental dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, except a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"The director may require that the applicant’s rental application fee be returned.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history; and (2) A statement that the applicant, pursuant to subsection a. of this section, may provide evidence demonstrating inaccuracies within the applicant's criminal record","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction of former applicant after successful appeal of Fair Chance order","requirement":"If a housing provider's successful appeal overturns a director's order that placed an applicant in a unit, that determination is grounds to evict the former applicant on at least 45 days' notice, notwithstanding the Anti-Eviction Act.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"A rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider that the former applicant occupies as the result of the director's order; rental dwelling units exclude owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Applies only where the tenant resides in the unit as the result of the director's order after the housing provider's successful appeal.","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Rental dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"then a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":"Applies notwithstanding any provision of the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.) to the contrary.","relations":[],"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
